    "id": "bihar-eou-blocks-over-20000-mobile-numbers-in-cybercrime-crackdown",
    "legacyId": 5305,
    "title": "Bihar EOU blocks over 20,000 mobile numbers in cybercrime crackdown",
    "summary": "A Digital Tsunami Hits Bihar The digital storm landed hard in Bihar—and this time, it wasn’t business as usual. The Economic Offences Unit (EOU) has deactivated over 20,000 mobile numbers, blocked more than 13,000 IMEIs, and frozen crores in bank accounts to clamp down on cybercrime. This decisive action shows Bihar is no longer a [&hellip;]",
    "content": "<h2 data-start=\"946\" data-end=\"983\"><strong data-start=\"949\" data-end=\"981\">A Digital Tsunami Hits Bihar</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1359\">The digital storm landed hard in Bihar—and this time, it wasn’t business as usual. The Economic Offences Unit (EOU) has <strong data-start=\"1104\" data-end=\"1146\">deactivated over 20,000 mobile numbers</strong>, blocked more than <strong data-start=\"1166\" data-end=\"1182\">13,000 IMEIs</strong>, and frozen crores in bank accounts to clamp down on cybercrime. This decisive action shows Bihar is no longer a passive victim—it’s fighting back with precision and purpose.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"1361\" data-end=\"1364\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"1366\" data-end=\"1421\"><strong data-start=\"1369\" data-end=\"1419\">Inside the Crackdown: The Numbers Tell a Story</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"1422\" data-end=\"1642\">From January to September 2025, Bihar logged around <strong data-start=\"1474\" data-end=\"1508\">74,000 online fraud complaints</strong>. The EOU responded decisively, freezing <strong data-start=\"1549\" data-end=\"1565\">₹75.92 crore</strong>—just over 21% of reported losses—and returning <strong data-start=\"1613\" data-end=\"1628\">₹5.14 crore</strong> to victims.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1644\" data-end=\"1988\">In October alone, <strong data-start=\"1662\" data-end=\"1684\">249 mobile numbers</strong> linked to online scams were deactivated. The department has also begun a rigorous investigation into “mule accounts,” which are bank accounts used to launder fraudulent money. In August, officials flagged nearly 200 such accounts and retrieved information on 138 of them through national data systems.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1990\" data-end=\"2189\">Furthermore, over <strong data-start=\"2008\" data-end=\"2047\">513 social media posts and profiles</strong> spreading misinformation or promoting scams have been removed. Every measure adds another layer of protection for Bihar’s digital citizens.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"2191\" data-end=\"2194\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"2196\" data-end=\"2231\"><strong data-start=\"2199\" data-end=\"2229\">Why This Crackdown Matters</strong></h2>\n<h3 data-start=\"2233\" data-end=\"2279\"><strong data-start=\"2237\" data-end=\"2277\">1. Rising Threats in the Digital Era</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"2280\" data-end=\"2544\">Bihar’s growing internet reach has brought new challenges. While access improves lives, it also exposes users to phishing, fake investment schemes, and online job scams. Many victims come from semi-urban and rural backgrounds, where digital literacy remains low.</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"2546\" data-end=\"2577\"><strong data-start=\"2550\" data-end=\"2575\">2. A Statewide Impact</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"2578\" data-end=\"2801\">Cybercrime isn’t confined to Patna or urban centers. Small towns and villages have also faced the brunt of fraudsters targeting unsuspecting users. This crackdown sends a clear message—no corner of Bihar is off the radar.</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"2803\" data-end=\"2838\"><strong data-start=\"2807\" data-end=\"2836\">3. Building Digital Trust</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"2839\" data-end=\"3068\">The EOU’s ongoing actions reinforce public faith in the system. By tracking transactions, blocking devices, and freezing suspicious accounts, authorities are restoring confidence in online financial activity and digital safety.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"3070\" data-end=\"3073\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"3075\" data-end=\"3131\"><strong data-start=\"3078\" data-end=\"3129\">Step-by-Step: How the EOU Is Winning the Battle</strong></h2>\n<ul data-start=\"3132\" data-end=\"3555\">\n<li data-start=\"3132\" data-end=\"3214\">\n<p data-start=\"3134\" data-end=\"3214\"><strong data-start=\"3134\" data-end=\"3161\">Mobile number blocking:</strong> Over 20,000 SIM cards linked to scams deactivated.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3215\" data-end=\"3288\">\n<p data-start=\"3217\" data-end=\"3288\"><strong data-start=\"3217\" data-end=\"3235\">IMEI lockdown:</strong> More than 13,000 mobile devices rendered unusable.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3289\" data-end=\"3389\">\n<p data-start=\"3291\" data-end=\"3389\"><strong data-start=\"3291\" data-end=\"3322\">Mule account investigation:</strong> Hundreds of suspicious bank accounts flagged and data retrieved.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3390\" data-end=\"3474\">\n<p data-start=\"3392\" data-end=\"3474\"><strong data-start=\"3392\" data-end=\"3410\">Fund recovery:</strong> ₹75.92 crore frozen, ₹5.14 crore already returned to victims.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3475\" data-end=\"3555\">\n<p data-start=\"3477\" data-end=\"3555\"><strong data-start=\"3477\" data-end=\"3505\">Social media monitoring:</strong> Over 500 misleading profiles and posts removed.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"3557\" data-end=\"3641\">Each of these steps pushes Bihar closer to a secure and accountable digital space.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"3643\" data-end=\"3646\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"3648\" data-end=\"3683\"><strong data-start=\"3651\" data-end=\"3681\">What It Means for Citizens</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"3684\" data-end=\"3945\">Every digital user in Bihar plays a role in this transformation. Awareness and caution are now vital weapons. Avoid sharing OTPs, clicking unknown links, or trusting random investment calls. If a message or transaction feels suspicious, report it immediately.</p>\n<p data-start=\"3947\" data-end=\"4152\">This campaign proves something powerful—<strong data-start=\"3987\" data-end=\"4033\">when technology is misused, Bihar will act</strong>. With the EOU leading from the front, the message is unmistakable: cybercriminals can no longer hide behind screens.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"4154\" data-end=\"4157\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"4159\" data-end=\"4211\"><strong data-start=\"4162\" data-end=\"4209\">Follow BiharSay — Your Window to Real Bihar</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"4212\" data-end=\"4409\">For more such impactful updates, grassroots stories, and inspiring news from Bihar, follow <strong data-start=\"4303\" data-end=\"4351\"><a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"https://www.biharsay.com\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"4305\" data-end=\"4349\">www.biharsay.com</a></strong> and become part of our <strong data-start=\"4375\" data-end=\"4406\">13k-strong global community</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"4411\" data-end=\"4779\"><strong data-start=\"4411\" data-end=\"4423\">BiharSay</strong> is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through stories of culture, innovation, and human change. With 13,000+ followers, high engagement across platforms, and the flagship <strong data-start=\"4648\" data-end=\"4661\">BiharCast</strong> series, BiharSay is the digital voice of Bihar—authentic, insightful, and proudly rooted in the heart of the state.</p>\n",
