    "id": "patna-sahib-eco-friendly-diwali-2025-11000-diyas-to-light-up-takht-shri-harmandir",
    "legacyId": 5288,
    "title": "Patna Sahib Eco-Friendly Diwali 2025 – 11,000 Diyas to Light Up Takht Shri Harmandir",
    "summary": "Patna Sahib to Glow with 11,000 Diyas This Diwali – A Unique Eco-Friendly Celebration at Takht Shri Harmandir Patna Sahib to Shine with 11,000 Diyas This Diwali – Celebrate Bandi Chhor Divas in an Eco-Friendly Way A Bandi Chhor Divas Like Never Before This year, Patna Sahib will witness a spectacular celebration as Takht Shri [&hellip;]",
    "content": "<h1 data-start=\"222\" data-end=\"357\">Patna Sahib to Glow with 11,000 Diyas This Diwali – A Unique Eco-Friendly Celebration at Takht Shri Harmandir</h1>\n<h3 data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"311\">Patna Sahib to Shine with 11,000 Diyas This Diwali – Celebrate Bandi Chhor Divas in an Eco-Friendly Way</h3>\n<hr data-start=\"313\" data-end=\"316\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"801\" data-end=\"847\"><strong data-start=\"804\" data-end=\"845\">A Bandi Chhor Divas Like Never Before</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"849\" data-end=\"1218\">This year, Patna Sahib will witness a spectacular celebration as <strong data-start=\"914\" data-end=\"938\">Takht Shri Harmandir</strong> is lit with <strong data-start=\"951\" data-end=\"967\">11,000 diyas</strong> for Bandi Chhor Divas. The festival isn’t just about lights; it’s a conscious effort to promote <strong data-start=\"1064\" data-end=\"1093\">eco-friendly celebrations</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1125\">environmental awareness</strong>. Devotees from across India are preparing with excitement to be part of this unique event.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1223\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"1225\" data-end=\"1264\"><strong data-start=\"1228\" data-end=\"1262\">Eco-Friendly Diwali Initiative</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"1266\" data-end=\"1597\">The <strong data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1304\">gurudwara management committee</strong> has introduced an innovative approach to this year’s celebrations. All 11,000 diyas are <strong data-start=\"1393\" data-end=\"1419\">traditional clay lamps</strong>, reducing environmental impact. The initiative encourages communities to celebrate <strong data-start=\"1503\" data-end=\"1525\">Diwali sustainably</strong>, spreading a powerful message of <strong data-start=\"1559\" data-end=\"1575\">green living</strong> alongside devotion.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"1602\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"1604\" data-end=\"1635\"><strong data-start=\"1607\" data-end=\"1633\">Religious Significance</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"1637\" data-end=\"1990\">Bandi Chhor Divas marks the historic release of <strong data-start=\"1685\" data-end=\"1709\">Guru Hargobind Sahib</strong>, the sixth Sikh Guru, from Gwalior Fort by Emperor Jahangir. Guru Sahib also freed 52 other kings, demonstrating compassion and justice. Since then, Sikhs commemorate this day by lighting diyas, praying, and holding community gatherings, blending history and spiritual devotion.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"1992\" data-end=\"1995\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"1997\" data-end=\"2046\"><strong data-start=\"2000\" data-end=\"2044\">Special Programs at Takht Shri Harmandir</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"2048\" data-end=\"2339\">On Bandi Chhor Divas, Takht Shri Harmandir will host <strong data-start=\"2101\" data-end=\"2140\">bhajan-kirtan, spiritual discourses</strong>, and a <strong data-start=\"2148\" data-end=\"2166\">special langar</strong> for devotees. Sikh families from all over India participate, creating a vibrant and united celebration that highlights the festival’s religious and cultural significance.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"2341\" data-end=\"2344\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"2346\" data-end=\"2381\"><strong data-start=\"2349\" data-end=\"2379\">Tradition of Diyas at Home</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"2383\" data-end=\"2650\">Families bring a <strong data-start=\"2400\" data-end=\"2445\">lit diya from their home to the gurudwara</strong>, then light all other diyas at home with it. This sacred flame is believed to bring <strong data-start=\"2530\" data-end=\"2566\">happiness, prosperity, and peace</strong>. Homes are also decorated with <strong data-start=\"2598\" data-end=\"2609\">rangoli</strong>, adding color and joy to the festival.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"2652\" data-end=\"2655\" />\n<h2 data-start=\"2657\" data-end=\"2686\"><strong data-start=\"2660\" data-end=\"2684\">Join the Celebration</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"2688\" data-end=\"2904\">Be part of this <strong data-start=\"2704\" data-end=\"2738\">eco-friendly Bandi Chhor Divas</strong> and witness Takht Shri Harmandir illuminated by 11,000 diyas. Carry the flame of devotion and awareness back to your home, and celebrate <strong data-start=\"2876\" data-end=\"2901\">tradition sustainably</strong>.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"2906\" data-end=\"2909\" />\n<p data-start=\"2911\" data-end=\"3221\"><strong data-start=\"2911\" data-end=\"2930\">Call to Action:</strong><br data-start=\"2930\" data-end=\"2933\" />Follow <a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"http://www.biharsay.com\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"2940\" data-end=\"2983\">www.biharsay.com</a> for regular updates, inspiring stories, and more initiatives from Bihar. Become part of the <strong data-start=\"3076\" data-end=\"3100\">13K global community</strong>! Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media platform, sharing stories on culture, grassroots change, and tradition.</p>\n",
